{
  "id": "m23l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "deque y namedtuple",
    "en": "deque and namedtuple"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Cola eficiente y registros ligeros"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`deque` (doble cola) añade y quita por **ambos extremos** de forma eficiente, y puede **rotar**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from collections import deque",
          "d = deque([1, 2, 3])",
          "d.appendleft(0)",
          "d.rotate(1)",
          "print(list(d))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[3, 0, 1, 2]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`namedtuple` crea una tupla con **campos con nombre**: ligera como una tupla, pero legible como un objeto."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from collections import namedtuple",
          "Punto = namedtuple('Punto', ['x', 'y'])",
          "p = Punto(1, 2)",
          "print(p.x, p.y)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "deque es la estructura correcta para colas (FIFO) y para historiales con tamaño máximo (maxlen)."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Efficient queue and lightweight records"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`deque` (double-ended queue) adds and removes from **both ends** efficiently, and can **rotate**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from collections import deque",
          "d = deque([1, 2, 3])",
          "d.appendleft(0)",
          "d.rotate(1)",
          "print(list(d))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[3, 0, 1, 2]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`namedtuple` creates a tuple with **named fields**: light as a tuple, readable as an object."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from collections import namedtuple",
          "Punto = namedtuple('Punto', ['x', 'y'])",
          "p = Punto(1, 2)",
          "print(p.x, p.y)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "deque is the right structure for queues (FIFO) and for capped histories (maxlen)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m23l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Crea un `namedtuple` llamado `Punto` con campos `x` e `y`.",
        "en": "Create a `namedtuple` named `Punto` with fields `x` and `y`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from collections import namedtuple",
        "",
        "# define Punto"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from collections import namedtuple",
        "",
        "Punto = namedtuple('Punto', ['x', 'y'])"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "namedtuple('Punto', ['x', 'y'])."
        ],
        "en": [
          "namedtuple('Punto', ['x', 'y'])."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "Punto",
          "harness": "p = Punto(1, 2)\nassert p.x == 1 and p.y == 2\nassert tuple(p) == (1, 2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m23l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `rotar(lista, n)` que devuelva la lista rotada `n` posiciones a la derecha (usa deque.rotate).",
        "en": "Define `rotar(lista, n)` returning the list rotated `n` positions to the right (use deque.rotate)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from collections import deque",
        "",
        "def rotar(lista, n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from collections import deque",
        "",
        "def rotar(lista, n):",
        "    d = deque(lista)",
        "    d.rotate(n)",
        "    return list(d)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Mete la lista en un deque, rótalo y vuelve a list()."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Put the list in a deque, rotate it and convert back to list()."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "rotar",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3,
                  4
                ],
                1
              ],
              "expected": [
                4,
                1,
                2,
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3
                ],
                0
              ],
              "expected": [
                1,
                2,
                3
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}